      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "It was found that in patients with attenuated tuberculous spondylitis and post-tuberculous vertebral osteochondrosis there was a sharp increase in platelet aggregability and a decrease in their disaggregability at the peak of the pain syndrome. With the therapy followed by relief of the pain syndrome, a rise in the platelet aggregability was significantly less noticeable, without significant changes in their disaggregability."},
